    <outcome date="2026-10-03" branch="task/uac-r2-132" base="3a6b38cb1b3acd6c3a14968b073be03793f37a59">
CODE-COMPLETE. OWNER SIGN-OFF = rounds 3 R3/R4 (BINDING, relayed as the merge gate): every residual bound is &lt;= 4 min (owner rule &lt;= 5 min). ESCALATION 7 FIRED (degraded RPA-fallback answer uncached during an RPA outage can more than double RPA volume) — recorded with options, code left at the classification rule's default (uncached), NOT cached for 60 s. Dev deploy + manual live gate (criterion 21) PENDING. Full record: notes/task-132-access-cache-faults-and-staleness.md (§0 anchors, §1 classification spec, §2-§5 per cache, §4 deny-veto trace, §6 invalidation, §7 TTLs + read volume, §8 escalation 7, §9 residual table, §10 tests, §11 perturbations, §12 manual gates, §13 placement).

BRANCH: task/uac-r2-132 from task/uac-r2-137-b2 (task 137, verified, not yet integrated), merged with work/unified-access-control-r2 cleanly (merge 3a6b38cb1, no conflicts); BFF built green before any change.

WHAT CHANGED: (a) GRANT SET — ExternalGrantSet.Faulted (internal init, JsonIgnore); QueryGrantSetAsync maps non-2xx / no value array / exception / timeout to ExternalGrantSet.Unreadable, rethrows only the CALLER's cancellation; the org-grant term returns (rows, faulted) and task 109's junction Unreadable marks the set faulted (no second read); GetGrantSetAsync (the one write path 137 left) never writes a faulted set. No CacheVersion bump (cached shape unchanged); 131's guard names Faulted in NotCarriedByDesign + a hit-never-faulted test. (b) IDENTITY — every sub-read returns (value, faulted); PersonIdentity.Faults (internal, not serialized — /api/users/me/memberships unchanged); cached only when nothing faulted; every touched catch guarded; CacheVersion 1 -> 2; TTL 10 -> 2 min. OrganizationMembershipResolver's identity seam now lets a query fault reach the identity layer (it was swallowed first, so the resolver-fault arm was unreachable). (c) MEMBERSHIP — one gate (TrySetCacheUnlessFaultedAsync): no cache write over a faulted identity or an unreadable people-targeting app-user check; CacheVersion 4 -> 5; TTL 5 -> 2 min; cache ids composed by one builder (ComposeCacheId). (d) SNAPSHOTS — AccessSnapshot.Faulted (additive, default false); DataverseAccessDataSource classifies OBO failure, user-lookup fault vs not-found, RPA unanswered -> probe readable (DEGRADED), probe 403/404 (answer) vs other/exception/timeout (fault) via one ClassifyProbeStatus, team/role sub-read faults; caller cancellation propagates; GetDataverseTokenViaOBOAsync internal virtual (test seam). CachedAccessDataSource: one gate (CacheUnlessFaulted); dead roles/teams keys + TTL fields deleted; ADR-009 PATH C — keys on ITenantCache under the caller tid (auth-access / auth-record-access, v1); no tid = no caching (no sentinel). (e) IMPERSONATED ROOT SETS — TTL 5 -> 2 min; still positive-only. DENY VETO — trace CONFIRMED (faulted systemuser row -> null contact -> ResolveDenyVetoAsync checks nothing); WorkforcePrincipal.ContactUnreadable (from PersonIdentity.ContactUnreadable or a thrown identity resolution) makes the systemuser plane deny every candidate; a contact READ as absent composes exactly as before. INVALIDATION — IMembershipCacheInvalidator gains InvalidateUserAccessAsync (identity + membership + root sets of one user) and InvalidateRecordOwnerChangeAsync (every user's membership + root sets for the entity type, every user's snapshot of the record): SCAN + DEL in the shared Redis, every tenant segment, no HttpContext needed, never throws, patterns built from the readers' own builders (TenantCache.BuildKey internal + AnyTenant + OnWire). Called from RegistrationDataverseService team add / remove / BU bind (only for this BFF's own Dataverse:ServiceUrl environment, D-13) and from ProvisionProjectEndpoint / UnsecureProjectEndpoint after the re-own (finally blocks). XML docs name the hook as the one every owner/team/BU writer (C10: 144, 146, 148, 149) must call.

DEFECT FOUND (ADR-032 tension): MembershipModule selected the real invalidator on Enabled AND services.Any(IConnectionMultiplexer), but Program.cs calls AddMembership BEFORE AddCacheModule, so the real invalidator could never be registered in any environment — turning the flag on in Bicep would have changed nothing. DECIDED: correctness does not depend on a kill switch — registration re-keyed on Redis:Enabled (the value CacheModule decides by); the junction publish + subscriber still follow Membership:CacheInvalidator:Enabled; Null peer only with an in-memory cache (Development/Testing). Deployed stacks already set Redis__Enabled=true (customer.bicep:606, model1-shared.bicep:520, model2-full.bicep:255); no Bicep change. Inert halves log once (Warning) at construction.

ESCALATION TRIGGERS: 1 (owner sign-off) — answered by owner R3/R4. 2 (read volume &gt; 2x) does not fire: worst point 1.88x (R = 30 req/h, notes §7). 3 (no tid) does not fire: every decorator caller is an HTTP request with a validated Entra token. 4 does not fire: a successful-read signal distinguishes unlinked users. 5 does not fire: Spaarke.Dataverse has no consumer outside the BFF. 6 does not fire: 109 merged. 7 FIRES — see above and notes §8 (options: keep uncached [recommended, implemented] vs a &lt;= 10 s TTL for the degraded answer). 8 does not fire: dev Redis &lt;= 178 keys (Azure Monitor totalkeys, 7 days, read-only).

109 RESIDUALS: (1) faulted-junction grant set cached for one TTL — CLOSED. (2) second junction read on a grant-set cache miss — ACCEPTED with reason (the cache-hit path already has the identical divergence for the full 60 s TTL; unifying would not tighten the worst case).

PLACEMENT (CLAUDE.md §10): in the BFF, in place — existing caches, the existing shared access data source, the existing invalidator interface; no new endpoint, service, interface, DI registration, option, job, column or package; the DI change re-keys an existing symmetric registration. THREE-QUESTION JUSTIFICATIONS (§11): fault indicators on existing types — existing ActiveOrgMemberships.Unreadable / ReferencedOrganizations.Unreadable / RootRecordFlags.Unreadable; extension: additive fields, internal where a contract would widen; cost: a 429 cached as "no grants" 60 s, a team-read fault hiding team-owned matters ~15 min, an unknown contact skipping the ethical wall. Eviction members — existing IMembershipCacheInvalidator + subscriber SCAN, IdentityNormalizationService.InvalidateAsync (current tenant only); extension: two members on the existing interface and its Null peer; cost: a secured project stays visible to BU colleagues for the TTLs, a removed team member keeps team-owned records.

STEP 9.5: code-review + adr-check over every changed file. Fixed: SCAN page size 250 -> 1000 (fewer round trips on a large keyspace); an unused test parameter. Accepted/recorded: a systematic systemuser-row read failure now denies the whole systemuser plane (criterion 16's fail-closed rule — depends on task 141's schema, live in dev); per-entity membership eviction also drops contact-plane entries for that entity type (harmless); environment comparison is string-based (trimmed, case-insensitive). ADR-003 fail-closed everywhere; ADR-009 path C (tenant keys, subject segment); eviction deletes tenant-scoped keys through IConnectionMultiplexer as the existing subscriber does (no IDistributedCache call); ADR-010 no new interface; ADR-013 membership types are not AI-internal (ArchTest forbids IOpenAiClient / IPlaybookService only; existing precedent); ADR-032 symmetric; ADR-038 no Mock of HttpMessageHandler, no path-A handler needed, no DI/ctor tests, no reflection. No violation.

TESTS: new AccessCacheFaultCachingTests (49), AccessCacheInvalidationTests (9), InMemoryRedisKeyspace harness; AccessCacheCharacterizationTests re-keyed; GrantCacheRoundTripSeamTests +1; ctor sites updated (incl. the integration project's SpyMembershipCacheInvalidator). Perturbations 15 seeded, all red, restored byte-identical, touched (notes §11). Suite results in notes §10 / this task's structured report.

PENDING MANUAL GATES: G-1 deploy the BFF to dev (bff-deploy skill); G-2 criterion 21 live gate (notes §12: MDA reassign of a team-owned test matter, poll within 4 min; warm-cache colleague + provision/re-secure, first request after return must not list it, direct read denied; record ExternalAccess:ImpersonatedRootSets:Enabled = off, 036 not merged); G-3 owner choice on escalation 7; G-4 publish size (skipped by instruction; no package change).
