BATCH 4 INTEGRATION RESIDUALS (both CLOSED). Full record: notes/task-132-access-cache-faults-and-staleness.md §16. Status completed-with-escalation -&gt; completed: escalation 7 was answered by owner round 10 item 3 (the degraded RPA-fallback answer stays uncached, as built); only the live manual gates G-1 (dev deploy) and G-2 (criterion 21) remain, unchanged (§12).

(1) SHARE-ONLY CHANGES EVICT LIKE OWNER CHANGES. Census: 8 files / 23 POA write sites, all through IDataverseRecordShareService (the four named paths plus the Assigned-To materializer, the No Access enforcer, Direct-thread and playbook sharing). The ONE POA seam, DataverseRecordShareService, now calls the new IMembershipCacheInvalidator.InvalidateRecordShareChangeAsync after every Grant/Modify/RevokeAccessAsync, in a finally (a thrown or cancelled write may have committed), with CancellationToken.None, never throwing or changing the write's outcome. It evicts every user's impersonated root set for the root type (a team share reaches every member) and every user's snapshots of the record (record-scoped; document-scoped too for sprk_documents). Not membership: a share is not a membership term. The document snapshot id is normalised (DocumentIdSegment, CachedAccessDataSource.CacheVersion 1 -&gt; 2) so the eviction reaches it however the request spelled the id; the owner-change hook gained the document pattern too. PoaShareClientSingletonGuardTests now fails the build on a POA write that bypasses the seam (per named writer file) or uses the SDK POA messages. [CORRECTED in f1-v1: this claim was false as first written — the f1 detector saw only a bare-identifier receiver, so verifier seeds S5 (sp.GetRequiredService&lt;DataverseWebApiService&gt;().RevokeAccessAsync(...)) and S6 (a same-named DataverseWebApiService parameter) stayed green. See the f1-v1 outcome below and notes §16.6.]

(2) NO EVICTION SCAN FOR A TYPE NO CACHE HOLDS. Premise corrected: the root-set pattern provably matched nothing for a cascade child, but the membership cache COULD hold one (GET /api/users/me/memberships/{entityType} takes any entity; discovery includes ownerid) and nothing stopped a record snapshot of one. Fixed by construction: AssignCascadeChildOwners.IsReownedByCascade / IsReownedByCascadeEntitySet (one declaration beside TablesFor) -&gt; MembershipResolverService.CachesEntityType (both planes) and CachedAccessDataSource.CachesRecordEntitySet never cache sharepointdocumentlocation / sharepointdocument; the hooks build each pattern only when its cache can hold the type, and EvictAsync returns before touching Redis with no pattern. A child restore: 0 patterns, 0 SCANs; a root owner change: still 3. The forward Assign cascade (never evicted) can no longer leave a stale child entry either.

PLACEMENT (CLAUDE.md §10): in the BFF, in place — the existing POA seam, the existing invalidator interface + its real and Null implementations, the existing caches. No new service, class, endpoint, option, job, column, PCF, package or DI registration (DataverseRecordShareService's existing registration resolves two added singleton dependencies). No plugin (ADR-002); fail closed unchanged (ADR-003). JUSTIFICATION (§11) for the one new member InvalidateRecordShareChangeAsync: existing = InvalidateRecordOwnerChangeAsync and ImpersonatedRootSetSource.InvalidateAsync (per user, caller's tenant only, one caller); extension = a member on the existing interface (reusing the owner hook would wipe every user's membership for the type on every share; the root-set helper cannot reach snapshots or other tenants); cost of doing nothing = an unshare or No Access revoke keeps the removed user's access via the cached root set (2 min) and snapshot (60 s), a new share is denied for the same windows, and every child of a fan-out keeps a stale snapshot. New internal predicates are members of the classes whose rule they state; DataverseAccessDataSource.DocumentEntitySetName became public (additive; no consumer outside the BFF). No .claude edit needed.

TESTS: AccessCacheInvalidationTests.Shares.cs (13 new cases: share-pattern reach x2, the production seam over the production DataverseWebApiService against an in-memory Web API x6 + cancellation + eviction-failure, cascade-child no-pattern x2, never-cached x1) and PoaShareClientSingletonGuardTests (+11: seam-only rule, one case per writer file x8, SDK-message rule, detector controls). PERTURBATIONS: 14 seeded (F1-F10 behaviour, F11-F14 a compiling bypass in each named path file), every one red, all restored byte-identical and touched (notes §16.4). RESULTS: build 0/0; BFF unit 15,430 passed / 0 failed / 54 skipped (15,484); NetArchTest 606/0/0; Sprk.Bff.Api.IntegrationTests 104/0/0; Spe.Integration.Tests 403 passed / 0 failed / 25 skipped (428). No package change.

