ROUND g — the lane's LAST fix round (owner round 56). Binding: main-session rounds 48 and 55 (work/unified-access-control-r2 note, read through round 58) and owner round 56 (NOTE-FROM-MAIN.md, not committed): fix classes (a)-(c), record (d)-(f) as Known limits, no new machinery for (d)-(f). Status stays completed: only G-1 / G-2 (live) and criterion 17's PR-time approval remain. Full record: notes §16.9 and "Known limits".

ROUND 55 (1) — THE EVICTION MOVES INTO THE WRITE. Spaarke.Dataverse gains ONE hook, IRecordShareWriteObserver (+ the RecordShareWrite kind). DataverseWebApiService.GrantAccessAsync / ModifyAccessAsync / RevokeAccessAsync send through one private method whose finally notifies the observer for the record the write addressed, on every path (returned, refused, thrown, cancelled), on CancellationToken.None; an observer fault is logged and never changes the write's outcome. The observer is a REQUIRED constructor argument. BFF: IMembershipCacheInvalidator extends the observer with a default member forwarding to InvalidateRecordShareChangeAsync; MembershipModule registers it unconditionally (real with Redis, the Null peer with the in-memory cache: ADR-032 symmetric); GraphModule passes it to the client. DataverseRecordShareService no longer evicts: ONE eviction path, one eviction per write.

ROUND 55 (2) — GUARDS STAY, CLAIMS TRUE. C3 re-targeted from the seam to the client's share-write sender (IlPathScan every-path proof: send awaited, then the notification for the sender's own entitySetName / recordId, awaited; the notification found in the IL; IlPathScan gains OpeningKeysFromSource). C1 / C2 / T1 keep task 060's single seam (no eviction claim). C7 bans exactly its list (test renamed NoCompiledCodeReferencesTheListedReflectionApis); it does NOT ban every reflective choice or invocation (seeds V, M — Known limits). Rewritten to the truth: the guard header, C7 doc / message, IlCallScan remarks, the seam's and invalidator's remarks, the Shares test summary, the controls' C7 summary, notes §16.8 (corrections appended), the f1-v1c-v1 outcome above (correction appended), and every comment / doc that said "the POA seam evicts" (caching-architecture.md x2 rows, uac-access-control.md, membership-resolution-pattern.md, CachedAccessDataSource, MembershipCacheInvalidator, ImpersonatedRootSetSource, two test doubles).

ROUND 55 (3) — C8 OVER EVERY src/server PROJECT. C8 reads each src/server assembly's compiled custom-attribute table (System.Reflection.Metadata; 8 projects, the newest bin/{config}/{tfm}/**/{name}.dll, failing loud on one not built); a new ArchTests target builds the L2 Worker and L2 test project. It replaces the reflection walk (one mechanism). Seed U5 (the attribute name spelled with a C# Unicode escape, in the L2 Worker): C8 red, T6 green (T6's claim corrected to "the text as written").

ITEMS (class per owner round 56): 1 rounds 48 / 55 — done above. 2, 3 (seeds V, M) — the eviction gap was class (a), closed at the root: behaviour tests ShareWrite_InvokedByALateBinderFromARunTimeName_StillEvictsThatRecord and ShareWrite_ResolvedFromItsMetadataTokenAndRunByALinqProvider_StillEvictsThatRecord; the C7 gap is class (d), recorded. 4 (comments contradict code) — class (b), fixed. 5 (more bans) — class (d), not built. 6 (U5) — class (d), fixed as round 55 (3) decided. 7, 8, 10, 11 — met. 9 — this round changes production IL: publish size measured. 15 (G-1 / G-2) — live, unchanged. 16 (criterion 17) — PR time, unchanged.

OVER-ENGINEERING CHECK: a refusal of share-write URLs in the client's private generic POST was built and REVERTED (it closed only a class-(d) route); not built: more C7 bans, T6 escape decoding. New surface (§11 three questions in notes §16.9): IRecordShareWriteObserver + RecordShareWrite; one forwarding DI registration; one required constructor parameter; IlPathScan.OpeningKeysFromSource; the ArchTests build target. No package, service class, endpoint, option, job, column or plugin.

